1
00:00:18,768 --> 00:00:22,146
Darrin Farr. Chief of police.
Welcome. You Agent Lisbon?

2
00:00:22,355 --> 00:00:24,148
- Yeah. This is Patrick Jane.
- Hey!

3
00:00:24,982 --> 00:00:27,985
Thanks for coming.
I've never called in CBI before.

4
00:00:28,694 --> 00:00:30,112
Interested to see your work.

5
00:00:31,531 --> 00:00:36,661
Okay, victim's name is Lucy Greene.
She was killed last night around 11:00.

6
00:00:37,078 --> 00:00:38,996
- Throat was slit.
- Charming.

7
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:40,873
She had an army I.D. on her.

8
00:00:41,832 --> 00:00:43,543
Says she's active duty.

9
00:00:43,876 --> 00:00:46,128
Corporal. Probably stationed
at Fort Runyon.

10
00:00:48,506 --> 00:00:49,924
That's about 2 miles
from here, right?

11
00:00:50,049 --> 00:00:52,593
Yeah. Soldiers from the base
come into town all the time.

12
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:55,304
If the coroner's not here
how did you know the time of death?

13
00:00:55,846 --> 00:00:58,015
The 9-1-1 call came in at 11:00.

14
00:00:58,224 --> 00:01:00,059
Fella said that a woman
had just been killed

15
00:01:00,268 --> 00:01:01,352
across the street from the church.

16
00:01:01,978 --> 00:01:03,729
- The caller give his name?
- No.

17
00:01:04,021 --> 00:01:06,857
Operator asked him to wait
while she dispatched the car.

18
00:01:07,066 --> 00:01:08,776
When she got back on the line,
he was gone.

19
00:01:11,153 --> 00:01:13,072
- What's that?
- The army.

20
00:01:13,990 --> 00:01:15,032
I figured that.

21
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:23,874
- Chief Farr?
- Yeah?

22
00:01:24,208 --> 00:01:26,586
Lieutenant Averill Lewis
Bravo company, second platoon.

23
00:01:26,961 --> 00:01:28,004
Thanks for notifying us.

24
00:01:29,755 --> 00:01:30,798
Oh, damn.

25
00:01:31,549 --> 00:01:32,800
All right, chief,
we'll take the case from here.

26
00:01:32,925 --> 00:01:34,760
These men are from our criminal
investigation division.

27
00:01:35,177 --> 00:01:36,762
If your officers will let them
have the crime scene?

28
00:01:36,887 --> 00:01:39,890
Lieutenant?
I'm Agent Lisbon with the CBI.

29
00:01:40,349 --> 00:01:41,392
We're handling this.

30
00:01:41,767 --> 00:01:44,395
Ma'am, all due respect, Corporal Greene
was a medic in my platoon.

31
00:01:44,604 --> 00:01:45,688
This is our responsibility.

32
00:01:45,938 --> 00:01:49,358
I understand why you would feel that way
but this is our case.

33
00:01:49,984 --> 00:01:51,986
Chief Farr, REGS
make this your call, right?

34
00:01:53,362 --> 00:01:56,324
Well, I kind of expected your agency
to send more than two people.

35
00:01:56,657 --> 00:01:59,410
- Our staff is on its way.
- Our team is here, Chief.

36
00:01:59,910 --> 00:02:01,621
They've closed homicides
on four continents.

37
00:02:01,746 --> 00:02:03,789
That's a good slogan. Four continents.
What, these guys?

38
00:02:05,249 --> 00:02:07,043
They look like they never
left Salt Lake City.

39
00:02:07,793 --> 00:02:09,587
- Who are you?
- Me? I'm with her.

40
00:02:10,588 --> 00:02:13,758
Lisbon, you used to play clarinet, right?
What is that tune?

41
00:02:22,183 --> 00:02:23,225
Yeah.

42
00:02:24,894 --> 00:02:26,395
It's "Kansas City."

43
00:02:27,271 --> 00:02:28,314
"Kansas City."

44
00:02:29,357 --> 00:02:31,192
- How does that go?
- You know...

45
00:02:35,946 --> 00:02:37,865
"Goin' to Kansas City"

46
00:02:38,366 --> 00:02:40,993
- "Kansas City, here I come"
- "Oh. here I come"

47
00:02:41,202 --> 00:02:44,246
- "They got some crazy little women there"
- "They got some crazy little women there"

48
00:02:44,372 --> 00:02:46,582
- "And I'm gonna..."
- "And I'm gonna get me..."

49
00:02:46,707 --> 00:02:48,000
She's very good.
That's very good.

50
00:02:48,793 --> 00:02:50,461
"Kansas City."
It's a classic blues tune.

51
00:02:50,795 --> 00:02:53,673
She's a fan of the blues.
Is there a blues club around here?

52
00:02:54,048 --> 00:02:56,050
Cat's Blues bar.
It's a couple blocks away.

53
00:02:56,300 --> 00:02:57,843
- Well, that's where she was.
- Or not.

54
00:03:00,221 --> 00:03:01,389
Take a look at her left hand.

55
00:03:03,099 --> 00:03:04,141
I'm looking.

56
00:03:04,517 --> 00:03:06,352
If you looked a little closer
than you're looking

57
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:09,355
you would see
a slight discoloration.

58
00:03:09,772 --> 00:03:10,815
It's not easy to see

59
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:12,775
but if you put that hand
under a U.V. light

60
00:03:12,983 --> 00:03:16,612
you would clearly see a small
but stylized picture of a pink cat

61
00:03:16,821 --> 00:03:17,947
stamped on that hand.

62
00:03:18,114 --> 00:03:20,658
Just like the ones they use
at the door of bars and clubs.

63
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:23,994
Hence Cat's Blues bar.
Thank you.

64
00:03:26,956 --> 00:03:28,874
Lieutenant, I think we can handle this.

65
00:03:30,251 --> 00:03:31,669
Looks that way to me.

66
00:03:33,254 --> 00:03:34,296
If that's your decision.

67
00:03:36,590 --> 00:03:37,925
- Let's go.
- Okay.

68
00:03:41,137 --> 00:03:43,931
They got some crazy
little women there...

69
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:45,975
- All right. Stop that now.
- Army of two.

70
00:03:57,551 --> 00:03:59,428
What do we know
about Lucy Greene?

71
00:04:00,137 --> 00:04:03,223
She was born and raised in New Jersey.
Her parents still live there.

72
00:04:03,599 --> 00:04:04,975
Talked to them.
They were pretty shook up.

73
00:04:05,309 --> 00:04:07,269
Said she seemed pretty happy
the last time they spoke.

74
00:04:07,478 --> 00:04:09,104
She joined the army after 9/11.

75
00:04:09,271 --> 00:04:11,690
Came back from Afghanistan
with her unit about two months ago

76
00:04:11,815 --> 00:04:13,692
- and received an army commendation.
- What for?

77
00:04:13,942 --> 00:04:16,028
She stabilized two wounded soldiers
and hid them from insurgents

78
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:18,405
until they could be evac'd.
She was a good soldier.

79
00:04:18,656 --> 00:04:19,698
{\an8}Sounds like it.

80
00:04:19,990 --> 00:04:21,784
{\an8}What about the mystery 9-1-1 caller?

81
00:04:21,992 --> 00:04:24,203
{\an8}Well, the phone records confirm
that the call came from a pay phone

82
00:04:24,328 --> 00:04:25,371
{\an8}near where the body was found.

83
00:04:25,496 --> 00:04:27,081
{\an8}Supposed to get a recording
of the call later on today.

84
00:04:27,206 --> 00:04:28,290
{\an8}- E-mail it to me.
- Okay.

85
00:04:28,415 --> 00:04:29,500
{\an8}Did the victim have any close friends?

86
00:04:29,708 --> 00:04:32,961
{\an8}Yeah. Her, uh, emergency contact
is another medic in the platoon.

87
00:04:33,253 --> 00:04:34,296
Rose Sutfin.

88
00:04:34,421 --> 00:04:35,631
{\an8}Jane and I will go talk to her.

89
00:04:35,881 --> 00:04:37,966
{\an8}Go to town, check out the bar
she was drinking at.

90
00:04:38,342 --> 00:04:40,803
- Who's our liaison at Fort Runyon?
- Lieutenant Lewis.

91
00:04:41,428 --> 00:04:42,471
Great.

92
00:04:50,354 --> 00:04:51,980
Corporal Greene
worked at the hospital.

93
00:04:52,147 --> 00:04:54,149
{\an8}Most of the medics work there
in some capacity.

94
00:04:54,942 --> 00:04:56,360
{\an8}Look, I want you to know
there are no hard feelings

95
00:04:56,527 --> 00:04:57,778
{\an8}about the disposition
of the case

96
00:04:57,903 --> 00:04:59,863
{\an8}but I'd appreciate being informed
of any developments.

97
00:05:00,114 --> 00:05:02,533
{\an8}We'll do our best.
How well did you know Lucy?

98
00:05:02,741 --> 00:05:05,494
{\an8}Not well. I only assumed command
of the platoon a few months ago.

99
00:05:07,955 --> 00:05:09,832
{\an8}Corporal Sutfin
is doing inventory in here.

100
00:05:12,668 --> 00:05:13,711
{\an8}Thank you.

101
00:05:14,169 --> 00:05:15,713
{\an8}This your first significant command?

102
00:05:16,588 --> 00:05:18,632
{\an8}Yes. It shows, does it?

103
00:05:19,591 --> 00:05:20,634
Ah, just a little.

104
00:05:23,303 --> 00:05:24,346
Corporal Sutfin.

105
00:05:25,764 --> 00:05:26,974
{\an8}- Sir.
- Ma'am.

106
00:05:27,516 --> 00:05:28,559
{\an8}At ease, Corporal.

107
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:31,687
These are the investigators
I spoke with you about.

108
00:05:31,854 --> 00:05:32,896
You'll assist them
with anything they ask.

109
00:05:33,272 --> 00:05:34,314
Yes, sir.

110
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:38,944
{\an8}- Which is Lucy's locker?
- Number 116.

111
00:05:39,153 --> 00:05:40,195
{\an8}Yeah?

112
00:05:41,864 --> 00:05:44,241
{\an8}There. I had maintenance
open it for you.

113
00:05:44,908 --> 00:05:45,951
{\an8}Ah, thank you.

114
00:05:47,077 --> 00:05:48,203
{\an8}How long had you known Lucy?

115
00:05:48,954 --> 00:05:49,997
{\an8}A couple of years.

116
00:05:50,497 --> 00:05:52,458
{\an8}Since my first tour in Afghanistan.

117
00:05:53,292 --> 00:05:57,337
{\an8}- What was she like?
- Smart. Real disciplined.

118
00:05:59,256 --> 00:06:00,716
{\an8}Lucy didn't have to learn
from mistakes.

119
00:06:01,633 --> 00:06:02,676
She didn't make them.

120
00:06:02,801 --> 00:06:04,762
{\an8}Well, discipline
always comes with a price.

121
00:06:06,221 --> 00:06:07,264
{\an8}What did she
have trouble with?

122
00:06:08,766 --> 00:06:09,933
{\an8}People, I guess.

123
00:06:10,309 --> 00:06:11,935
{\an8}Guys in the unit, mostly.

124
00:06:13,437 --> 00:06:15,981
{\an8}She'd be the first to tell you
she was O.C.D. about the rules.

125
00:06:16,106 --> 00:06:18,442
{\an8}Real detail-oriented.

126
00:06:18,776 --> 00:06:21,653
She'd point out if you messed up
and that doesn't go down well.

127
00:06:22,279 --> 00:06:23,322
Especially with guys.

128
00:06:23,739 --> 00:06:26,116
{\an8}- You defended her?
- I tried to.

129
00:06:27,493 --> 00:06:28,702
She looked out for me.

130
00:06:29,495 --> 00:06:31,413
Anything unusual
happen recently?

131
00:06:32,247 --> 00:06:35,667
{\an8}Um... someone
was sending her flowers.

132
00:06:36,627 --> 00:06:37,669
Someone at the clinic.

133
00:06:39,171 --> 00:06:41,715
She wouldn't say who it was
and I think she was a little weirded out.

134
00:06:42,090 --> 00:06:43,133
{\an8}What clinic?

135
00:06:43,258 --> 00:06:45,427
{\an8}The T.B.I. and psychological
health clinic.

136
00:06:45,803 --> 00:06:47,596
{\an8}When she wasn't here,
she worked there.

137
00:06:48,305 --> 00:06:50,432
{\an8}You should talk to Dr. Bowman.
Her was her supervisor.

138
00:06:51,141 --> 00:06:52,434
Excuse me.

139
00:06:54,937 --> 00:06:55,979
Is that it?

140
00:06:57,064 --> 00:06:58,106
Oh, pretty much.

141
00:06:58,357 --> 00:07:00,859
Uh, you know, unless you wanna
talk about that other thing.

142
00:07:01,902 --> 00:07:02,945
What's that?

143
00:07:04,029 --> 00:07:05,614
The thing that you didn't want me
to ask you about.

144
00:07:06,782 --> 00:07:08,116
I don't know what that is.

145
00:07:11,078 --> 00:07:12,120
Well, neither do I.

146
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:16,542
Nice to meet you, Rose.

147
00:07:22,714 --> 00:07:25,509
Rigsby just sent over a copy
of the 9-1-1 call. Listen to this.

148
00:07:27,094 --> 00:07:29,346
"Medic... I need a medic, ASAP.
Lucy's hurt."

149
00:07:29,555 --> 00:07:30,973
"Calm down, sir.
Where are you?"

150
00:07:31,139 --> 00:07:33,433
"I'm... uh, I'm on
Wyoga Lake Avenue."

151
00:07:33,684 --> 00:07:36,061
"20 meters north of the church
the St. Sebastian."

152
00:07:36,311 --> 00:07:37,896
"Somebody just cut her throat.
There's blood all over."

153
00:07:38,063 --> 00:07:40,440
"Okay sir, I need you to hold a moment
while I dispatch a car."

154
00:07:40,649 --> 00:07:42,442
- "Will you do that?"
- "Yeah. I'll wait."

155
00:07:42,693 --> 00:07:43,735
"Thank you, sir."

156
00:07:45,070 --> 00:07:46,822
"Hello, sir? Now can you
tell me your name?"

157
00:07:47,865 --> 00:07:49,950
"Hello? Sir? Are you there?"

158
00:07:50,701 --> 00:07:52,744
"He knows her well enough
to call her Lucy"

159
00:07:52,870 --> 00:07:54,288
"and he's very worried
about her."

160
00:07:54,872 --> 00:07:57,374
"But then it seems like he just walks away.
It's weird, isn't it?"

161
00:07:59,501 --> 00:08:02,588
"ASAP". "20 meters".
he's a soldier.

162
00:08:03,672 --> 00:08:06,091
- "We don't open till 6:30."
- "CBI."

163
00:08:07,885 --> 00:08:08,927
Well, then we're open.

164
00:08:10,220 --> 00:08:11,263
Was this woman
here last night?

165
00:08:11,722 --> 00:08:14,349
Yeah. Louise.
No... Lucy.

166
00:08:15,142 --> 00:08:16,935
- What'd she do?
- She was murdered.

167
00:08:17,936 --> 00:08:20,355
- Get out. Seriously? Murdered?
- Yes.

168
00:08:21,815 --> 00:08:24,568
Yeah. She's here
two, three times a week.

169
00:08:24,985 --> 00:08:26,945
- She loves the music.
- Did she come with anyone?

170
00:08:27,654 --> 00:08:28,989
No. Comes by herself.

171
00:08:29,907 --> 00:08:31,491
She did get in an argument
with these soldiers.

172
00:08:31,617 --> 00:08:34,828
They were hassling her.
Couldn't tell you what it was about.

173
00:08:34,995 --> 00:08:37,164
Now, these other soldiers...
you know their names?

174
00:08:37,581 --> 00:08:39,499
Nope. They were in
the Night Wolves unit.

175
00:08:40,208 --> 00:08:41,501
Had the patch on their clothes.

176
00:08:42,252 --> 00:08:44,004
That's her unit.
Her own people were hassling her?

177
00:08:44,212 --> 00:08:48,091
Yeah. Well, it wouldn't surprise me.
The Night Wolves guys are trouble.

178
00:08:49,134 --> 00:08:51,595
- Take after their sergeant.
- You know his name?

179
00:08:51,845 --> 00:08:55,307
- Yeah.
- Hawkins. Sergeant Hawkins.

180
00:09:02,189 --> 00:09:03,231
Sergeant Hawkins?

181
00:09:04,274 --> 00:09:05,317
Yes, sir, I am.

182
00:09:07,110 --> 00:09:08,904
Kimball Cho. CBI.
A word in private?

183
00:09:13,283 --> 00:09:15,911
- Is this about Greene?
- Yes. What can you tell me about her?

184
00:09:17,162 --> 00:09:19,539
Outstanding soldier.
Vital part of the platoon.

185
00:09:19,665 --> 00:09:21,124
It's a... tragedy.

186
00:09:21,291 --> 00:09:22,793
How'd she get along
with the rest of the squad?

187
00:09:23,251 --> 00:09:25,420
- No problems.
- Did she have any enemies?

188
00:09:25,545 --> 00:09:28,465
Enemies? No.
I mean, people fight.

189
00:09:28,757 --> 00:09:31,343
In my unit, we work it out
and put it behind us.

190
00:09:32,010 --> 00:09:34,471
I don't let bad feelings fester.
It takes a unit apart.

191
00:09:35,013 --> 00:09:37,057
Do you know why Lucy was arguing
with some squad mates last night?

192
00:09:38,225 --> 00:09:39,267
That's the first I've heard.

193
00:09:39,476 --> 00:09:41,520
A witness says some of your men
were arguing with Corporal Greene

194
00:09:41,645 --> 00:09:42,688
at a bar last night.

195
00:09:43,313 --> 00:09:45,023
Maybe they are mistaken.

196
00:09:45,816 --> 00:09:46,858
I don't think so.

197
00:09:47,025 --> 00:09:48,068
I'm gonna have to talk to your men.

198
00:09:49,736 --> 00:09:52,656
You be my guest, Agent Cho.
You be my guest.

199
00:09:59,913 --> 00:10:01,373
- Dr. Bowman?
- Yes?

200
00:10:01,999 --> 00:10:03,625
Teresa Lisbon. Patrick Jane.

201
00:10:04,376 --> 00:10:06,586
We're looking into the death
of Lucy Greene.

202
00:10:06,795 --> 00:10:08,922
Oh, of course.

203
00:10:10,298 --> 00:10:11,758
Have a seat, please.

204
00:10:15,470 --> 00:10:16,513
It's terrible.

205
00:10:17,055 --> 00:10:18,223
On top of everything else

206
00:10:18,348 --> 00:10:20,892
Lucy's death's been
a real blow to the program.

207
00:10:21,101 --> 00:10:22,602
She was a tremendous asset.

208
00:10:23,061 --> 00:10:24,104
What's the program?

209
00:10:24,521 --> 00:10:28,191
We treat returning soldiers for T.B.I.
traumatic brain injury.

210
00:10:28,608 --> 00:10:31,361
And other mental health issues
that result from combat.

211
00:10:32,362 --> 00:10:34,948
- Must be busy.
- Unfortunately, yes.

212
00:10:35,073 --> 00:10:37,993
There are a lot of people returning home
with serious problems.

213
00:10:38,452 --> 00:10:41,329
And even minor T.B.I.
can produce sleep deprivation

214
00:10:41,455 --> 00:10:43,540
emotional issues,
memory impairment.

215
00:10:44,249 --> 00:10:46,668
- What did Lucy do?
- She was a battle buddy

216
00:10:46,960 --> 00:10:51,214
a medic, uh, paired with one patient
for the course of treatment.

217
00:10:52,132 --> 00:10:53,175
She was great at it.

218
00:10:53,508 --> 00:10:56,762
Very detail-oriented
but also a huge heart.

219
00:10:57,721 --> 00:10:59,723
So you must have fought with her.
Did you?

220
00:10:59,848 --> 00:11:00,891
Why do you say that?

221
00:11:01,099 --> 00:11:03,769
Well, you're a man who's
used to being obeyed

222
00:11:03,977 --> 00:11:05,437
and she wasn't afraid
to speak her mind.

223
00:11:05,562 --> 00:11:06,688
There must have been
some fireworks.

224
00:11:07,147 --> 00:11:09,608
No. We disagreed sometimes.
That happens.

225
00:11:09,983 --> 00:11:12,402
Well, I imagine you've been
under a great deal of stress

226
00:11:12,527 --> 00:11:13,570
since the divorce?

227
00:11:14,321 --> 00:11:15,614
How do you know I'm divorced?

228
00:11:17,032 --> 00:11:20,410
Well, there's
a... number of signs.

229
00:11:21,787 --> 00:11:26,041
I mean, the obvious is,
the overuse of cologne.

230
00:11:26,750 --> 00:11:28,835
You could probably afford to be
a little less liberal with that.

231
00:11:29,503 --> 00:11:30,962
Making my eyes water.

232
00:11:32,172 --> 00:11:33,757
Well... thanks for the tip.

233
00:11:34,132 --> 00:11:35,509
It's been a little over a year.

234
00:11:35,634 --> 00:11:37,969
I'm doing quite fine, actually,
thanks for asking.

235
00:11:38,261 --> 00:11:39,304
- Good.
- Great.

236
00:11:39,596 --> 00:11:41,389
"Code Red in building 21A."

237
00:11:41,640 --> 00:11:43,642
"Code Red in building 21A."

238
00:11:43,892 --> 00:11:45,644
"Emergency personnel, please respond."

239
00:11:46,019 --> 00:11:48,396
- Uh, what's a Code Red?
- A fire.

240
00:11:48,605 --> 00:11:49,731
It... it's in another building.

241
00:11:49,898 --> 00:11:53,068
The medics on duty in the hospital
act as the base's E.M.T.s

242
00:11:53,235 --> 00:11:55,028
so they make
an announcement in here.

243
00:11:55,821 --> 00:11:57,155
Is... is there anything else?

244
00:11:57,280 --> 00:11:59,533
Because I have patients to see.

245
00:12:00,534 --> 00:12:02,994
Doc? A little help?

246
00:12:03,370 --> 00:12:04,454
Speech and memory class.

247
00:12:04,621 --> 00:12:06,706
Down the hall left,
and left again.

248
00:12:06,998 --> 00:12:08,041
Want someone
to go with you?

249
00:12:08,583 --> 00:12:09,960
I got it. Thanks.

250
00:12:12,879 --> 00:12:14,131
Memory impairment?

251
00:12:14,589 --> 00:12:16,299
Short-term memory's
a real problem.

252
00:12:16,466 --> 00:12:18,468
Things they've seen or heard
just drop out.

253
00:12:18,885 --> 00:12:20,679
- If you'll excuse me.
- Sure.

254
00:12:25,350 --> 00:12:27,435
- Well, come on.
- Why? Where?

255
00:12:28,019 --> 00:12:31,231
Our 9-1-1 caller may not
have run away from the phone.

256
00:12:32,065 --> 00:12:33,650
He may have forgotten about it.
Let's go.

257
00:12:33,942 --> 00:12:35,694
So we're gonna do
an association exercise

258
00:12:35,819 --> 00:12:37,779
using the cards
that you found on your chairs.

259
00:12:37,904 --> 00:12:39,322
It's all about
making connection.

260
00:12:39,614 --> 00:12:42,325
Re-educating the brain
to put things together.

261
00:12:42,659 --> 00:12:45,579
If I were to show you a picture
like this one

262
00:12:46,246 --> 00:12:48,540
I want you to show me
the picture from your cards...

263
00:12:48,665 --> 00:12:51,585
- That matches or... Yes?
- Sorry for the interruption.

264
00:12:51,877 --> 00:12:54,337
I'm Patrick Jane, this is Teresa Lisbon.
We're with the CBI.

265
00:12:54,462 --> 00:12:56,673
We're investigating the murder
of Lucy Greene.

266
00:12:57,340 --> 00:12:58,508
And how can we help you?

267
00:12:58,758 --> 00:13:00,927
We have a recording
made the night of the murder.

268
00:13:01,052 --> 00:13:03,180
Does anyone recognize this voice?

269
00:13:03,638 --> 00:13:04,848
"I'm... I'm on Wyoga Lake Avenue..."

270
00:13:05,265 --> 00:13:07,517
"20 meters north of the church...
the St. Sebastian."

271
00:13:07,642 --> 00:13:09,269
"Somebody just cut her throat.
There's blood all over."

272
00:13:09,477 --> 00:13:11,897
"Okay sir, I need you to hold a moment
while I dispatch a car."

273
00:13:12,105 --> 00:13:13,190
- "Will you do that?"
- "Yeah."

274
00:13:14,316 --> 00:13:16,443
That's my voice. That's me.

275
00:13:18,528 --> 00:13:20,447
- What's your name?
- Pete Coen.

276
00:13:22,115 --> 00:13:23,408
I don't remember any of that.

277
00:13:23,992 --> 00:13:26,203
Pete, we need to talk to you.
Could you come with me, please?

278
00:13:26,828 --> 00:13:29,122
- Yeah, guess.
- Yeah, that's fine, Pete.

279
00:13:29,623 --> 00:13:30,665
Okay.

280
00:13:39,216 --> 00:13:40,258
Thank you.

281
00:13:42,844 --> 00:13:43,887
All of you.

282
00:13:47,140 --> 00:13:48,183
Very much.

283
00:13:53,328 --> 00:13:55,455
- "I'll wait."
- "Thank you, sir."

284
00:13:57,457 --> 00:13:59,459
"Hello, sir?
Now can you tell me your name?"

285
00:14:00,752 --> 00:14:03,254
"Hello? Sir? Are you there?"

286
00:14:04,422 --> 00:14:06,966
"You forgot why you were there
and you just walked away."

287
00:14:08,217 --> 00:14:09,344
Sounds like something I'd do.

288
00:14:11,304 --> 00:14:15,224
We found a date-stamped receipt
from a taco truck in your wallet.

289
00:14:15,808 --> 00:14:17,810
It parks down the street
from the crime scene.

290
00:14:18,394 --> 00:14:20,229
It's dated from the night of the killing.

291
00:14:22,065 --> 00:14:23,566
What were you doing in town?

292
00:14:24,108 --> 00:14:27,779
Walking. When... when I can't sleep,
I go on walks.

293
00:14:29,238 --> 00:14:31,366
The church is 2 miles from the base.

294
00:14:32,700 --> 00:14:34,077
I've got nothing else to do, ma'am.

295
00:14:34,619 --> 00:14:36,120
I like that church. I like the bells.

296
00:14:38,664 --> 00:14:41,042
Can you remember anything
that happened that night?

297
00:14:45,505 --> 00:14:46,547
No.

298
00:14:47,256 --> 00:14:48,299
I'm sorry.

299
00:14:49,175 --> 00:14:50,843
Well, what can
you remember, generally?

300
00:14:52,887 --> 00:14:55,640
Before the explosion's pretty good.
After that...

301
00:14:57,100 --> 00:14:58,518
And when was the... the explosion?

302
00:14:59,727 --> 00:15:01,229
11 months ago in AFFA.

303
00:15:02,480 --> 00:15:03,815
My squad was patrolling Khost.

304
00:15:05,733 --> 00:15:07,568
I got out of a Humvee
to eyeball an intersection.

305
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:10,363
I waved them through.

306
00:15:11,239 --> 00:15:14,742
And they went right over an I.E.D.

307
00:15:18,204 --> 00:15:20,540
I woke up three days later
in a hospital in Germany.

308
00:15:22,083 --> 00:15:23,126
The other guys...

309
00:15:25,503 --> 00:15:26,546
They...

310
00:15:28,423 --> 00:15:29,465
Now...

311
00:15:31,509 --> 00:15:33,636
My memory is... gone.

312
00:15:34,470 --> 00:15:36,347
I can't sleep.

313
00:15:36,472 --> 00:15:39,976
I... get angry and sad
and I have no idea why.

314
00:15:47,191 --> 00:15:48,943
- Is that to remind you?
- Yeah.

315
00:15:50,611 --> 00:15:51,654
"Take meds"

316
00:15:51,779 --> 00:15:54,198
which, of course,
I didn't remember.

317
00:15:57,368 --> 00:15:58,703
Government gave it to me.

318
00:15:59,787 --> 00:16:00,830
I'm supposed to...

319
00:16:04,083 --> 00:16:05,835
supposed to carry it with me
everywhere that I go.

320
00:16:06,419 --> 00:16:08,796
I have to write down everything
that I'm supposed to do.

321
00:16:09,297 --> 00:16:10,631
I have to write down everything
that I remember

322
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:13,384
even if it's in the middle of the night.
Like that helps.

323
00:16:14,510 --> 00:16:15,553
It's useless.

324
00:16:17,221 --> 00:16:21,809
Do you have a... reminder in here
to buy Lucy some flowers?

325
00:16:23,352 --> 00:16:24,479
How'd you know I did that?

326
00:16:25,646 --> 00:16:28,149
Oh, your voice on the 9-1-1 call

327
00:16:28,774 --> 00:16:30,651
sounded like you're a little more
than just friends.

328
00:16:34,030 --> 00:16:36,240
I spent a lot of time with Lucy
in the hospital.

329
00:16:37,575 --> 00:16:39,619
She was always really nice.

330
00:16:41,245 --> 00:16:42,371
You start to think...

331
00:16:43,122 --> 00:16:44,790
maybe there could be
something more, you know?

332
00:16:45,917 --> 00:16:46,959
And...

333
00:16:48,503 --> 00:16:51,923
She was nice about the whole thing but
I think more embarrassed than anything.

334
00:16:53,090 --> 00:16:54,425
Did Lucy make you angry?

335
00:16:54,884 --> 00:16:56,511
- Uh, I mean...
- Mr....

336
00:16:57,929 --> 00:16:58,971
Sorry.

337
00:17:03,893 --> 00:17:05,770
Did she? Make you angry?

338
00:17:07,271 --> 00:17:09,315
- Did who make me angry?
- Lucy?

339
00:17:10,566 --> 00:17:11,984
Lucy Greene?

340
00:17:12,109 --> 00:17:13,945
Why... why are we talking
about Lucy Greene?

341
00:17:14,070 --> 00:17:15,279
Did she... is she okay?

342
00:17:18,616 --> 00:17:21,118
Lucy's dead.
She was murdered.

343
00:17:23,037 --> 00:17:24,080
What?

344
00:17:29,961 --> 00:17:32,964
Do you think there's a chance
he'll remember anything from that night?

345
00:17:33,464 --> 00:17:35,591
Maybe. I-I don't know.

346
00:17:35,841 --> 00:17:39,512
- What time did the 9-1-1 call come in?
- Little bit after 11:00.

347
00:17:40,263 --> 00:17:41,305
Taco.

348
00:17:43,516 --> 00:17:45,518
- I need to go back to the crime scene.
- Why?

349
00:17:46,185 --> 00:17:47,228
Well, I want a taco.

350
00:17:57,029 --> 00:17:58,072
Excuse me.

351
00:17:58,406 --> 00:17:59,865
Where does the taco truck park?

352
00:18:00,116 --> 00:18:01,158
Uh, down that way.

353
00:18:01,284 --> 00:18:02,618
Won't be here
for a few hours, though.

354
00:18:02,952 --> 00:18:04,495
Well, I guess I'll have to wait.

355
00:18:07,248 --> 00:18:08,332
Gardenias.

356
00:18:10,585 --> 00:18:11,627
My favorite.

357
00:18:28,436 --> 00:18:30,229
Could Pete have killed her
and forgot he did it?

358
00:18:30,646 --> 00:18:31,772
It's not impossible.

359
00:18:31,981 --> 00:18:34,692
Go to the hospital and see if anybody
saw him come back that night.

360
00:18:34,817 --> 00:18:36,777
What condition he was in,
if he said anything.

361
00:18:37,445 --> 00:18:39,113
And search his room.
He agreed to it.

362
00:18:39,238 --> 00:18:40,656
- Sure.
- Rigsby...

363
00:18:41,449 --> 00:18:43,743
He may forget who you are
or why you're there.

364
00:18:43,868 --> 00:18:46,287
- Just explain what's going on gently.
- I got it.

365
00:18:47,330 --> 00:18:48,706
Where are we with Lucy's unit?

366
00:18:48,831 --> 00:18:50,333
Everyone in the platoon
agrees with Hawkins.

367
00:18:50,541 --> 00:18:52,293
Lucy was great.
Nobody had a problem with her.

368
00:18:52,668 --> 00:18:54,795
You think the waitress misunderstood
what was going on that night

369
00:18:54,920 --> 00:18:56,297
- or are they lying?
- No. They're lying.

370
00:18:57,131 --> 00:19:00,051
The hospital sent over a list
of patients Lucy worked with.

371
00:19:00,343 --> 00:19:02,970
The most recent one
was a guy named Jacob Lettner.

372
00:19:03,346 --> 00:19:04,764
- See what he has to say.
- Sure.

373
00:19:08,184 --> 00:19:09,935
{\an8}What exactly did Lucy do for you, Jacob?

374
00:19:10,311 --> 00:19:12,980
She helped me, keep track of medications
and appointments

375
00:19:13,731 --> 00:19:15,524
kept copies of my paperwork.

376
00:19:16,609 --> 00:19:17,652
When things got difficult

377
00:19:17,777 --> 00:19:20,071
she talked me down off the ledge.
Like that.

378
00:19:21,155 --> 00:19:22,448
Sounds like you were close.

379
00:19:24,533 --> 00:19:27,286
Yeah. We, uh... we weren't
dating or anything

380
00:19:27,411 --> 00:19:29,080
but... I liked her.

381
00:19:29,372 --> 00:19:30,414
When's the last time
you saw her?

382
00:19:30,956 --> 00:19:32,583
Well, I was almost done
with the program

383
00:19:32,792 --> 00:19:35,753
so I was only seeing her once a week.
Six days ago, I guess.

384
00:19:36,003 --> 00:19:37,922
- How'd she seem?
- Fine.

385
00:19:38,714 --> 00:19:40,216
Did she mention any problems
with the people in her unit?

386
00:19:42,093 --> 00:19:43,135
Come here.

387
00:19:49,809 --> 00:19:52,395
She, uh... she asked me not
to tell anyone about this.

388
00:19:52,561 --> 00:19:54,230
Like, begged me.

389
00:19:55,690 --> 00:19:57,316
If Lucy had a problem with somebody,
we need to know.

390
00:19:59,276 --> 00:20:00,820
Couple of weeks ago,
she was really upset...

391
00:20:01,487 --> 00:20:03,489
crying, which she never did.

392
00:20:04,990 --> 00:20:06,033
She told me she had filed

393
00:20:06,158 --> 00:20:07,410
a sexual harassment
report anonymously

394
00:20:07,535 --> 00:20:08,577
against someone
in the platoon.

395
00:20:09,453 --> 00:20:10,663
Somehow, some of the guys
found out

396
00:20:10,830 --> 00:20:11,872
and they were giving her
crap about it.

397
00:20:11,997 --> 00:20:13,040
What kind of crap?

398
00:20:13,958 --> 00:20:17,211
Just... you know,
stupid stuff... mean.

399
00:20:18,087 --> 00:20:20,423
- Who did she file the claim against?
- She wouldn't say.

400
00:20:20,548 --> 00:20:21,716
Well, who in the unit
was giving her trouble?

401
00:20:21,841 --> 00:20:24,719
I... I don't know names.
A lot of them.

402
00:20:26,470 --> 00:20:29,140
Sergeant Hawkins,
you lied.

403
00:20:29,598 --> 00:20:30,641
Not true.

404
00:20:30,766 --> 00:20:32,184
You said Lucy
had no problems with the squad

405
00:20:32,309 --> 00:20:33,352
but you knew
she was being punished

406
00:20:33,477 --> 00:20:34,979
because she filed
a sexual harassment complaint.

407
00:20:35,187 --> 00:20:36,230
I knew no such thing.

408
00:20:37,231 --> 00:20:39,191
I had no idea
who filed that complaint.

409
00:20:39,442 --> 00:20:41,902
Now, I was told by
the Inspector General's office

410
00:20:42,445 --> 00:20:44,029
that an anonymous complaint
had been filed

411
00:20:44,155 --> 00:20:45,489
against a soldier
in the platoon.

412
00:20:45,740 --> 00:20:47,658
I investigated
that accusation thoroughly.

413
00:20:47,992 --> 00:20:49,034
How'd you do that?

414
00:20:49,160 --> 00:20:50,911
I questioned every man
and woman in the unit.

415
00:20:51,120 --> 00:20:54,373
Not one said they had seen
or experienced any misconduct.

416
00:20:54,665 --> 00:20:57,084
No witnesses,
no intended victim

417
00:20:57,710 --> 00:20:59,712
no investigation,
so I closed it.

418
00:20:59,837 --> 00:21:01,255
You knew some men
were harassing Lucy

419
00:21:01,464 --> 00:21:02,506
for making the accusation.

420
00:21:02,757 --> 00:21:05,843
If they were, I never heard a word about it
and she never said a thing.

421
00:21:05,968 --> 00:21:09,054
She didn't have to. It's your unit.
It's your job to know what's going on.

422
00:21:10,389 --> 00:21:12,141
But you thought Lucy had become
a troublemaker, didn't you?

423
00:21:12,975 --> 00:21:14,810
You were hoping the backlash
would convince her to transfer.

424
00:21:16,687 --> 00:21:18,105
Is there a question there?

425
00:21:18,481 --> 00:21:19,982
Who was the original harassment
complaint against?

426
00:21:20,357 --> 00:21:21,400
I won't tell you that.

427
00:21:21,567 --> 00:21:23,152
You don't get to choose
which questions you answer.

428
00:21:23,402 --> 00:21:25,780
No? Well, you do
whatever you like.

429
00:21:25,946 --> 00:21:27,865
'Cause I'm not draggin' a good
officer's name through the mud

430
00:21:27,990 --> 00:21:29,283
so that you can go fishing.

431
00:21:33,120 --> 00:21:35,414
Any chance holding Hawkins
will change his mind?

432
00:21:35,539 --> 00:21:37,208
- No.
- Kick him loose, then.

433
00:21:38,042 --> 00:21:39,794
- Something seems off here.
- What?

434
00:21:40,336 --> 00:21:42,671
Everybody says that Lucy
was a stickler for the rules

435
00:21:42,922 --> 00:21:45,174
that she had no problem
speaking up for herself.

436
00:21:45,424 --> 00:21:48,052
But she gets harassed, and she
makes an anonymous complaint?

437
00:21:48,719 --> 00:21:50,554
And when the unit gives her
a hard time about it

438
00:21:50,679 --> 00:21:52,223
she doesn't say anything?

439
00:21:52,389 --> 00:21:53,432
That doesn't sound like her.

440
00:21:53,557 --> 00:21:54,975
Well, she told Lettner
she filed the complaint.

441
00:21:55,100 --> 00:21:56,143
Why would she lie?

442
00:21:56,268 --> 00:21:57,853
Maybe she wanted people
to think she filed it

443
00:21:57,978 --> 00:21:59,563
because she was
protecting someone else.

444
00:22:02,149 --> 00:22:03,609
With your permission, ma'am...

445
00:22:04,777 --> 00:22:05,820
What's this about?

446
00:22:06,737 --> 00:22:09,824
Rose, some people in the unit
think that Lucy filed

447
00:22:09,949 --> 00:22:12,910
an anonymous
sexual harassment complaint.

448
00:22:13,619 --> 00:22:15,996
I think she was taking the heat
for somebody else.

449
00:22:16,497 --> 00:22:17,540
Am I right?

450
00:22:19,375 --> 00:22:22,336
Does this have something to do
with why Lucy was killed?

451
00:22:23,045 --> 00:22:25,047
It might.
I don't know yet.

452
00:22:27,299 --> 00:22:28,676
Was she covering for you, Rose?

453
00:22:32,763 --> 00:22:33,806
Yes.

454
00:22:34,515 --> 00:22:37,309
There's a hotline
I called about four weeks ago.

455
00:22:38,769 --> 00:22:40,980
Please, don't tell my unit.
Please.

456
00:22:44,692 --> 00:22:46,944
You had to have known
an anonymous accusation

457
00:22:47,152 --> 00:22:48,487
was not gonna do much.

458
00:22:49,405 --> 00:22:52,950
I-I guess I hoped that when
the investigation started

459
00:22:53,075 --> 00:22:56,120
other people would come forward
so it wouldn't be just me.

460
00:22:57,454 --> 00:22:58,747
But that didn't happen.

461
00:22:59,832 --> 00:23:01,917
And when Hawkins
started the investigation

462
00:23:02,251 --> 00:23:03,711
people assumed it was Lucy?

463
00:23:04,920 --> 00:23:07,172
Because she was so hardcore
about the rules.

464
00:23:09,174 --> 00:23:10,968
She said it was okay,
that she could take it.

465
00:23:12,678 --> 00:23:13,721
But...

466
00:23:14,680 --> 00:23:16,015
I saw how much it hurt her.

467
00:23:18,225 --> 00:23:20,019
I just wanted
the whole thing to go away.

468
00:23:20,269 --> 00:23:23,439
So... when Hawkins
questioned me

469
00:23:23,564 --> 00:23:26,734
I... I said I didn't
know anything about it.

470
00:23:27,359 --> 00:23:28,402
Rose...

471
00:23:31,196 --> 00:23:32,323
Who did you name
in the complaint?

472
00:23:33,157 --> 00:23:34,199
Who harassed you?

473
00:23:36,243 --> 00:23:38,412
I-I can't talk about it.
It's against REGS.

474
00:23:40,372 --> 00:23:42,499
Hawkins told Cho that he didn't want

475
00:23:42,625 --> 00:23:45,210
to drag an officer's name
through the mud.

476
00:23:45,878 --> 00:23:47,421
An officer, not a soldier.

477
00:23:48,505 --> 00:23:49,840
It was Lewis, wasn't it?

478
00:23:50,591 --> 00:23:52,009
Lewis harassed you.

479
00:23:52,635 --> 00:23:54,678
I didn't...I didn't say that.
I'm not saying that.

480
00:23:54,845 --> 00:23:57,181
- Rose...
- Ma'am, I'd like to leave now.

481
00:23:57,640 --> 00:23:58,682
May I?

482
00:23:58,933 --> 00:24:01,060
- I can't stop you.
- Thanks.

483
00:24:08,651 --> 00:24:09,693
What's up, Rigsby?

484
00:24:10,611 --> 00:24:12,655
I searched Pete's room.
Didn't find anything.

485
00:24:12,821 --> 00:24:15,324
His clothes had been taken for washing
so I tracked 'em down in the laundry.

486
00:24:15,991 --> 00:24:17,034
And?

487
00:24:17,159 --> 00:24:19,411
Found a jacket.
There's bloodstains on it.

488
00:24:23,290 --> 00:24:26,377
Pete is my patient,
and, uh, very fragile.

489
00:24:26,502 --> 00:24:28,128
Do you really need to talk with him
again tonight?

490
00:24:28,629 --> 00:24:29,672
I do.

491
00:24:30,714 --> 00:24:32,549
Well, please keep the questions
short and simple.

492
00:24:32,675 --> 00:24:34,301
Last thing Pete needs
is more stress.

493
00:24:38,180 --> 00:24:39,390
Pete?

494
00:24:39,932 --> 00:24:41,517
Put on your shoes.
We're gonna go out.

495
00:24:42,017 --> 00:24:44,228
Oh, sure.
I'd like that.

496
00:24:49,984 --> 00:24:51,026
What is it, Jane?

497
00:24:51,151 --> 00:24:54,947
Uh, Lisbon... could you bring Pete Coen
to St. Sebastian church in, uh...

498
00:24:55,698 --> 00:24:59,493
- A little under an hour?
- We found blood on his clothes.

499
00:25:00,119 --> 00:25:01,745
I have to take him
to the office for a talk.

500
00:25:01,954 --> 00:25:02,997
Won't do you any good.

501
00:25:03,330 --> 00:25:04,456
You have a better idea?

502
00:25:04,581 --> 00:25:06,583
I'll see you in a little under an hour.
Be prompt.

503
00:25:23,434 --> 00:25:24,476
Jane, what's up?

504
00:25:24,601 --> 00:25:26,186
We're gonna try to restore Pete's memory.

505
00:25:26,520 --> 00:25:27,938
Well, a piece of it, at least.

506
00:25:30,858 --> 00:25:31,900
How could you do that?

507
00:25:32,192 --> 00:25:35,112
Ah, well, I'll explain. But first...
Oh, gracias, señor.

508
00:25:37,406 --> 00:25:39,116
- Taco?
- Sure, thanks.

509
00:25:39,491 --> 00:25:41,243
- Lisbon, you hungry?
- No, thank you.

510
00:25:41,368 --> 00:25:42,411
Okay.

511
00:25:42,953 --> 00:25:45,998
Uh, a memory can be brought back
by a word or an image

512
00:25:46,123 --> 00:25:49,084
but the best tools for digging one out
are the senses...

513
00:25:49,209 --> 00:25:51,628
smell, hearing, taste.

514
00:25:52,713 --> 00:25:54,882
So I'm eating a taco because
I ate one the night Lucy died?

515
00:25:55,007 --> 00:25:56,341
That's right. Taste is first.

516
00:25:56,467 --> 00:25:58,761
Second, coming from the taco truck

517
00:25:59,136 --> 00:26:02,681
you would have walked right by these
beautifully fragrant gardenias.

518
00:26:08,562 --> 00:26:11,565
Okay. I smell it,
but it's not doing anything.

519
00:26:12,566 --> 00:26:16,028
Then, right before the murder
you heard a very distinctive sound.

520
00:26:17,362 --> 00:26:18,405
And you will hear it...

521
00:26:21,784 --> 00:26:23,327
- What sound?
- Wait for it.

522
00:26:34,797 --> 00:26:36,048
- This is really...
- Shh...

523
00:26:39,218 --> 00:26:40,260
Pete?

524
00:26:43,388 --> 00:26:44,431
I remember.

525
00:26:54,481 --> 00:26:56,775
Don't force the memory.
Just... just let it come.

526
00:26:59,069 --> 00:27:00,112
I was here.

527
00:27:01,238 --> 00:27:03,323
"Just walking.
I heard a sound."

528
00:27:16,378 --> 00:27:17,420
Hey!

529
00:27:19,047 --> 00:27:20,090
I couldn't see anything.

530
00:27:20,757 --> 00:27:23,260
By the time my eyes adjusted,
the guy was gone.

531
00:27:23,677 --> 00:27:24,719
And Lucy...

532
00:27:27,722 --> 00:27:28,807
It's difficult, I know.

533
00:27:29,766 --> 00:27:31,059
It's very important to continue.

534
00:27:34,187 --> 00:27:35,647
"I tried to talk to her."

535
00:27:36,022 --> 00:27:37,732
Stay here. Stay here.
Stay with me.

536
00:27:37,941 --> 00:27:39,151
But her throat...

537
00:27:39,317 --> 00:27:40,485
Stay with me.

538
00:27:43,280 --> 00:27:44,781
"She just kept
squeezing my hand."

539
00:27:48,785 --> 00:27:50,453
Do you remember anything
about her killer?

540
00:27:50,704 --> 00:27:53,456
His race? His height?
His clothing? Anything?

541
00:27:53,582 --> 00:27:56,168
- I can't talk right now.
- Pete, I need your attention.

542
00:27:56,543 --> 00:27:57,711
I need to write this down.

543
00:27:59,462 --> 00:28:00,505
So I don't forget.

544
00:28:07,721 --> 00:28:10,473
It doesn't eliminate him as a suspect.
He could be lying.

545
00:28:12,976 --> 00:28:14,477
Fine. He's not a suspect.

546
00:28:14,895 --> 00:28:15,937
What else do we have?

547
00:28:16,271 --> 00:28:17,647
Well, Rigsby's got
Lucy's phone records.

548
00:28:17,772 --> 00:28:18,815
He's going through them.

549
00:28:18,940 --> 00:28:20,025
I think we should go after Lewis.

550
00:28:20,692 --> 00:28:22,819
- We don't have anything on him.
- Well, he harassed Rose.

551
00:28:23,153 --> 00:28:24,196
Maybe Lucy threatened him.

552
00:28:24,821 --> 00:28:26,615
Told him that she would have
the investigation reopened.

553
00:28:27,073 --> 00:28:28,116
Maybe.

554
00:28:29,034 --> 00:28:30,076
I agree with Cho.

555
00:28:30,410 --> 00:28:32,370
Man is begging
for some thumbscrews.

556
00:28:35,540 --> 00:28:38,293
You're seriously asking me where I was
when Corporal Greene was killed?

557
00:28:39,044 --> 00:28:40,462
- Answer the question.
- Why?

558
00:28:40,795 --> 00:28:42,380
You were accused
of sexual harassment.

559
00:28:43,006 --> 00:28:45,008
Lucy Greene knew the victim.
That made her dangerous to you.

560
00:28:45,342 --> 00:28:46,384
No, it didn't.

561
00:28:47,052 --> 00:28:48,303
Are you refusing
to answer the question?

562
00:28:50,305 --> 00:28:52,182
The army, in its infinite wisdom

563
00:28:52,307 --> 00:28:54,976
permits the anonymous reporting
of sexual harassment.

564
00:28:55,268 --> 00:28:57,145
Which means any nut
or idiot with an attitude

565
00:28:57,270 --> 00:28:58,605
can make trouble
free of charge.

566
00:28:59,564 --> 00:29:01,650
Some malcontent
made a wild accusation.

567
00:29:01,775 --> 00:29:04,778
It was investigated, nothing was found
there was no victim.

568
00:29:05,237 --> 00:29:06,279
I didn't do anything.

569
00:29:06,404 --> 00:29:08,281
You still haven't told me where you were
when Lucy Greene was killed.

570
00:29:09,491 --> 00:29:10,867
And we checked with
the front gate at the base.

571
00:29:11,034 --> 00:29:12,244
They said you left
in a hurry that day.

572
00:29:12,702 --> 00:29:13,745
I was late.

573
00:29:14,079 --> 00:29:16,665
Getting to a surprise party
for the base commander's wife.

574
00:29:16,998 --> 00:29:18,375
I was there until after midnight.

575
00:29:18,792 --> 00:29:20,168
About 30 people saw me there.

576
00:29:21,544 --> 00:29:22,629
Do you have
any other questions?

577
00:29:28,051 --> 00:29:29,302
Base commander's X.O. confirms

578
00:29:29,427 --> 00:29:31,888
Lewis was at his house until midnight.
Couldn't have done it.

579
00:29:32,681 --> 00:29:33,848
We're a little light on suspects.

580
00:29:34,599 --> 00:29:35,642
I may have something.

581
00:29:36,059 --> 00:29:37,352
Telephone records say
Jacob Lettner

582
00:29:37,477 --> 00:29:39,521
made a bunch of phone calls to
Lucy the day she was murdered.

583
00:29:40,105 --> 00:29:42,357
Well, Lettner told me he hadn't
spoken to Lucy in almost a week.

584
00:29:42,482 --> 00:29:45,360
- We better bring him in.
- I'll go. Someone I need to see.

585
00:29:45,527 --> 00:29:46,569
Okay.

586
00:29:50,198 --> 00:29:51,241
Hey.

587
00:29:52,701 --> 00:29:54,286
More questions, huh?

588
00:29:54,911 --> 00:29:56,329
Well, you got stamina.
I'll give you that.

589
00:29:56,579 --> 00:29:57,622
No questions.

590
00:29:59,374 --> 00:30:01,084
Your men were wrong
about Lucy.

591
00:30:01,584 --> 00:30:03,128
She didn't file
the sexual harassment charge.

592
00:30:03,336 --> 00:30:04,379
She was protecting
the person who did.

593
00:30:04,713 --> 00:30:05,755
Well, that's too bad.

594
00:30:06,589 --> 00:30:09,050
- But it doesn't change anything.
- It should.

595
00:30:09,426 --> 00:30:10,635
Reopen the investigation.

596
00:30:11,553 --> 00:30:13,013
If you don't, you're letting
Lewis off the hook.

597
00:30:13,805 --> 00:30:15,223
Reopen the investigation?

598
00:30:16,558 --> 00:30:17,851
Yeah, yeah, I'll do that.

599
00:30:18,435 --> 00:30:19,477
Why not?

600
00:30:19,602 --> 00:30:20,645
There's no evidence.

601
00:30:21,479 --> 00:30:22,522
He's a lieutenant.

602
00:30:22,647 --> 00:30:24,441
Do you know how fast
he could have a foot up my ass?

603
00:30:25,692 --> 00:30:27,652
All right.
I'm done here.

604
00:30:27,777 --> 00:30:28,820
Talk to Rose.

605
00:30:29,821 --> 00:30:31,197
- Sutfin?
- Just talk to her.

606
00:30:31,323 --> 00:30:34,367
I already did. She said she
didn't know boo about Lewis.

607
00:30:34,492 --> 00:30:36,453
She was scared.
Tell her you'll protect her.

608
00:30:36,578 --> 00:30:38,621
It's not my job
to hold anybody's hand.

609
00:30:38,747 --> 00:30:39,789
You don't have to.

610
00:30:39,914 --> 00:30:41,416
Just don't abandon her
like you abandoned Lucy.

611
00:30:43,335 --> 00:30:45,587
I didn't abandon anybody.

612
00:30:45,795 --> 00:30:46,880
You keep
telling yourself that.

613
00:30:47,964 --> 00:30:49,424
But the next time you ask
someone in this unit

614
00:30:49,549 --> 00:30:51,843
to watch your back, he might
remember how you watched hers.

615
00:30:56,431 --> 00:30:58,975
Jacob, tell us again about
the last time you saw Lucy.

616
00:30:59,100 --> 00:31:01,478
Like I... like I said, it was...
it was more than a week ago.

617
00:31:02,145 --> 00:31:03,563
We know that you spoke to her
on the phone

618
00:31:03,688 --> 00:31:05,648
several times a day
before she died.

619
00:31:06,733 --> 00:31:07,859
You're right.

620
00:31:08,234 --> 00:31:09,569
You're right. I'm sorry.
I forgot.

621
00:31:09,819 --> 00:31:11,363
No, you didn't.

622
00:31:12,447 --> 00:31:14,324
If you want to avoid
getting into trouble

623
00:31:14,449 --> 00:31:16,785
stop lying and tell us
the truth now.

624
00:31:17,202 --> 00:31:18,244
It was nothing.

625
00:31:18,578 --> 00:31:20,080
It was nothing.
It was about my meds.

626
00:31:20,580 --> 00:31:21,623
Well, what about them?

627
00:31:22,040 --> 00:31:23,500
I'm about to finish
the program.

628
00:31:24,000 --> 00:31:25,585
Move out on my own.

629
00:31:26,294 --> 00:31:28,380
But Lucy had to certify
that I was capable, you know

630
00:31:28,505 --> 00:31:29,839
that I could take care
of myself.

631
00:31:30,006 --> 00:31:31,132
Keeping on top
of your meds.

632
00:31:31,508 --> 00:31:32,550
Yeah.

633
00:31:34,302 --> 00:31:35,345
But that morning

634
00:31:35,553 --> 00:31:39,432
Lucy told me I'd messed up one of them
taken too little, and I hadn't.

635
00:31:40,225 --> 00:31:42,727
So I told her she made a mistake
which in Lucy's mind is...

636
00:31:44,187 --> 00:31:45,230
It's, like, impossible.

637
00:31:45,814 --> 00:31:46,856
Little miss detail.

638
00:31:48,566 --> 00:31:49,609
So we went a few rounds
on the phone

639
00:31:49,734 --> 00:31:51,861
but she finally agreed to double-check
the prescription records.

640
00:31:52,987 --> 00:31:54,697
Why didn't you tell us
about this earlier?

641
00:31:55,448 --> 00:31:56,825
Because if they think
I messed up my meds

642
00:31:56,991 --> 00:31:58,868
they won't let me live
on my own.

643
00:31:59,994 --> 00:32:01,037
It's wrong.

644
00:32:02,997 --> 00:32:04,040
Look, I'm...

645
00:32:04,374 --> 00:32:05,417
I'm ready.

646
00:32:07,210 --> 00:32:08,253
I am.

647
00:32:13,466 --> 00:32:16,177
Rigsby just talked to Jacob's
boss at the P.X.

648
00:32:16,428 --> 00:32:18,054
He was doing inventory
the night of the murder.

649
00:32:18,388 --> 00:32:19,806
This case is nothing
but dead ends.

650
00:32:19,931 --> 00:32:21,558
Yeah, not necessarily.
Do you have a padlock?

651
00:32:22,100 --> 00:32:24,018
- A padlock?
- Yeah. A lock with a key.

652
00:32:24,144 --> 00:32:26,354
I know what a padlock is, and, no
I do not have a padlock.

653
00:32:26,479 --> 00:32:27,814
Thank you. I'll ask the janitor.

654
00:32:32,277 --> 00:32:33,319
Come in.

655
00:32:35,697 --> 00:32:36,739
Hey.

656
00:32:36,865 --> 00:32:37,907
Mr. Jane.

657
00:32:38,491 --> 00:32:39,534
Is something wrong?

658
00:32:39,659 --> 00:32:41,661
Oh, no, I just had something to do
downstairs.

659
00:32:41,828 --> 00:32:43,913
I thought I'd stop by.
They're nice drawings.

660
00:32:44,414 --> 00:32:45,457
Oh, thanks.

661
00:32:47,041 --> 00:32:49,169
Wow. I know you have trouble
sleeping. I, uh...

662
00:32:49,961 --> 00:32:51,963
I know a technique
that may be helpful.

663
00:32:52,338 --> 00:32:53,381
What kind of technique?

664
00:32:54,174 --> 00:32:57,343
Ah, it's just, mild hypnosis.

665
00:32:58,094 --> 00:32:59,220
Just helps you relax.

666
00:32:59,804 --> 00:33:00,889
What do I have to do?

667
00:33:01,723 --> 00:33:03,057
Lie down and listen.

668
00:33:06,394 --> 00:33:07,437
Sure.

669
00:33:08,146 --> 00:33:09,230
I could really
use some sleep.

670
00:33:09,731 --> 00:33:12,317
- All right, well, just lie down.
- Okay.

671
00:33:14,110 --> 00:33:15,153
Close your eyes.

672
00:33:16,613 --> 00:33:17,655
Breathe.

673
00:33:18,072 --> 00:33:21,576
Fill your mind with all those thoughts
that keep you awake.

674
00:33:22,577 --> 00:33:24,579
Let them crowd around
behind your eyes.

675
00:33:26,456 --> 00:33:27,499
Good.

676
00:33:27,624 --> 00:33:28,750
Now I want you
to paint them black.

677
00:33:30,627 --> 00:33:31,836
Each one of them.

678
00:33:33,463 --> 00:33:34,923
Dark and heavy.

679
00:33:35,924 --> 00:33:37,091
All the same color.

680
00:33:39,594 --> 00:33:41,179
Each one is getting softer...

681
00:33:43,306 --> 00:33:44,349
and heavier.

682
00:33:45,099 --> 00:33:46,142
And quiet...

683
00:33:47,310 --> 00:33:48,728
and peaceful.

684
00:33:48,978 --> 00:33:50,021
And quiet...

685
00:33:52,982 --> 00:33:54,025
and peaceful.

686
00:34:12,210 --> 00:34:13,628
- You reach everyone?
- Yep.

687
00:34:13,753 --> 00:34:14,796
Good.

688
00:34:16,297 --> 00:34:18,591
Rigsby, we're a go
in five minutes.

689
00:34:19,968 --> 00:34:22,845
T-minus 5 minutes.

690
00:34:23,513 --> 00:34:24,556
Yep.

691
00:34:32,420 --> 00:34:33,463
What's this about?

692
00:34:33,629 --> 00:34:35,089
Well, we learned of some
evidence this morning

693
00:34:35,214 --> 00:34:36,799
- we need your help with.
- Our help?

694
00:34:37,483 --> 00:34:38,526
What evidence?

695
00:34:39,026 --> 00:34:41,112
Why don't we have Pete tell us?
He's the one who found it.

696
00:34:42,029 --> 00:34:43,072
Hey, what's up, Pete?

697
00:34:43,781 --> 00:34:45,241
I remembered something last night.

698
00:34:45,533 --> 00:34:46,742
I found it on my P.D.A.
this morning.

699
00:34:46,867 --> 00:34:48,661
I must have woken up in the middle
of the night and written it down.

700
00:34:48,911 --> 00:34:49,954
What did you remember?

701
00:34:52,081 --> 00:34:54,500
When Lucy took my hand,
she gave me a key.

702
00:34:54,667 --> 00:34:55,710
A key?

703
00:34:55,835 --> 00:34:57,044
I guess that's why she was
grabbing my hands

704
00:34:57,211 --> 00:34:59,922
so I searched my room,
and I found...

705
00:35:00,548 --> 00:35:01,591
This.

706
00:35:02,133 --> 00:35:03,467
- Can I see that?
- Yes, ma'am.

707
00:35:05,761 --> 00:35:07,263
Does this mean anything to anybody?

708
00:35:07,555 --> 00:35:09,181
- No.
- Not me.

709
00:35:09,849 --> 00:35:13,811
It looks like a medic's locker key
but 107's not Lucy's locker.

710
00:35:14,145 --> 00:35:15,688
Why would she have
another locker?

711
00:35:17,523 --> 00:35:18,566
Hide something.

712
00:35:18,733 --> 00:35:20,818
Well, maybe Lucy found
something incriminating

713
00:35:21,110 --> 00:35:24,113
decided to store it in the locker
and then she was killed for it.

714
00:35:24,238 --> 00:35:25,448
That's why she gave
the key to Pete.

715
00:35:25,573 --> 00:35:29,201
- Lewis, can we search the locker?
- Sure. With a warrant.

716
00:35:29,577 --> 00:35:31,579
- Oh, come on.
- It's my duty to go by the book.

717
00:35:31,746 --> 00:35:32,788
You need a warrant.

718
00:35:33,539 --> 00:35:34,957
It'll take me 20 minutes
to get one.

719
00:35:37,335 --> 00:35:38,586
Ah, Lewis.

720
00:35:40,713 --> 00:35:41,797
Such a stickler.

721
00:36:03,069 --> 00:36:04,528
It's just gonna be a little while longer.

722
00:36:05,821 --> 00:36:08,032
"Code Red in building 17D."

723
00:36:08,240 --> 00:36:10,242
"Code Red in building 17D."

724
00:36:10,534 --> 00:36:12,787
"All emergency personnel
respond immediately."

725
00:36:12,995 --> 00:36:14,538
That's me. Uh, sorry.

726
00:36:14,997 --> 00:36:18,125
Okay, well, thank you all for your help.
We'll let you know what we find.

727
00:36:24,298 --> 00:36:26,258
"Code Red in building 17D."

728
00:36:26,425 --> 00:36:28,219
"Code Red in building 17D."

729
00:36:28,844 --> 00:36:31,138
"All emergency personnel
respond immediately."

730
00:37:04,338 --> 00:37:06,340
Hey, Doc. What are you doin'?

731
00:37:08,843 --> 00:37:09,885
I...

732
00:37:10,469 --> 00:37:12,555
"Eh, uh, uh..."

733
00:37:13,305 --> 00:37:14,890
You're a silver-tongued devil.

734
00:37:19,311 --> 00:37:22,773
We found a significant number
of cash deposits in your account.

735
00:37:24,275 --> 00:37:25,776
You were writing
fake prescriptions

736
00:37:25,901 --> 00:37:28,237
and selling the drugs
under the table for cash.

737
00:37:29,238 --> 00:37:30,281
That's what Lucy found

738
00:37:30,406 --> 00:37:32,116
when she looked into
Jacob's prescription records.

739
00:37:32,491 --> 00:37:34,577
- Are you divorced, Agent?
- No.

740
00:37:35,953 --> 00:37:38,456
You have no idea
how expensive it is.

741
00:37:39,248 --> 00:37:42,585
I'm paying legal fees,
alimony, child support...

742
00:37:43,502 --> 00:37:45,713
And all so the lying bitch
can be supported

743
00:37:46,005 --> 00:37:47,715
in the manner to which
she's accustomed.

744
00:37:48,132 --> 00:37:49,967
What about the manner
to which I'm accustomed?

745
00:37:50,509 --> 00:37:51,594
What about my lifestyle?

746
00:37:53,345 --> 00:37:55,264
- And dating isn't cheap.
- Really?

747
00:38:00,060 --> 00:38:01,103
Lucy came to me.

748
00:38:03,314 --> 00:38:04,690
The diligent fool.

749
00:38:05,065 --> 00:38:07,902
Said she found some serious problems
with the prescriptions.

750
00:38:09,153 --> 00:38:11,113
No idea I was behind it, but...

751
00:38:11,614 --> 00:38:14,658
She's all gung ho to launch
a big investigation.

752
00:38:16,202 --> 00:38:17,244
That's how she was.

753
00:38:23,918 --> 00:38:26,420
"She said she was going
to the blues club that night, so..."

754
00:38:27,797 --> 00:38:28,923
"I waited down the street."

755
00:38:34,136 --> 00:38:35,179
Lucy?

756
00:38:36,138 --> 00:38:37,181
- Doctor?
- Yeah.

757
00:38:37,681 --> 00:38:38,724
What are you doing here?

758
00:38:38,849 --> 00:38:41,477
There's a man hurt back here.
Come and help me.

759
00:38:42,269 --> 00:38:43,312
Uh, okay. Sure.

760
00:38:44,980 --> 00:38:46,023
Only took a second.

761
00:38:55,491 --> 00:38:58,536
Takes about a minute to bleed to death
so I waited.

762
00:39:02,414 --> 00:39:03,457
Hey!

763
00:39:08,462 --> 00:39:09,839
This is not my fault.

764
00:39:10,381 --> 00:39:12,842
If my ex-wife had just agreed
to a reasonable settlement

765
00:39:12,967 --> 00:39:14,760
none of this would have happened.

766
00:39:15,803 --> 00:39:18,347
Oh, well...
look on the bright side.

767
00:39:19,390 --> 00:39:21,559
In prison, you won't
have to pay for dates.

768
00:39:33,612 --> 00:39:34,655
What are you doing here?

769
00:39:35,531 --> 00:39:37,283
- Just watching.
- Excuse me?

770
00:39:39,493 --> 00:39:40,536
Lieutenant Lewis.

771
00:39:45,082 --> 00:39:46,125
I need to speak with you.

772
00:39:46,500 --> 00:39:47,960
Later, Sergeant Hawkins.
I'm busy.

773
00:39:48,168 --> 00:39:50,754
No, sir. We need to do this ASAP.

774
00:39:51,297 --> 00:39:52,840
It's regarding a code violation.

775
00:39:58,178 --> 00:39:59,221
Are you serious?

776
00:40:00,347 --> 00:40:01,515
Sir, we have to go now.

777
00:40:06,270 --> 00:40:07,313
Hawkins.

778
00:40:28,626 --> 00:40:30,294
I got your message, Mr. Jane.

779
00:40:31,462 --> 00:40:32,504
- I'm sorry.
- No, it's...

780
00:40:32,630 --> 00:40:34,673
No. It's good. Good.

781
00:40:37,468 --> 00:40:40,220
Pete, thank you for coming by.

782
00:40:41,138 --> 00:40:45,893
I just... I wanted to apologize
for tricking you without asking.

783
00:40:47,561 --> 00:40:48,938
The gag wouldn't have
worked without it.

784
00:40:49,188 --> 00:40:50,230
Sorry.

785
00:40:51,482 --> 00:40:53,776
You got the guy who killed Lucy.
That's good enough for me.

786
00:40:57,154 --> 00:41:00,950
I'm... actually here
about that other thing.

787
00:41:03,077 --> 00:41:04,828
Do you really think you could
help restore my memory?

788
00:41:07,623 --> 00:41:10,709
Well, I do have a tool
that could be very useful.

789
00:41:11,418 --> 00:41:12,962
- Have a seat.
- All right.

790
00:41:18,550 --> 00:41:19,635
It's called a memory palace.

791
00:41:20,260 --> 00:41:22,888
It's basically a place
to connect memories to.

792
00:41:23,722 --> 00:41:26,308
You said I would need the image
of a place I knew really well.

793
00:41:26,433 --> 00:41:28,102
- Yes, that's right.
- I think I got one.

794
00:41:31,939 --> 00:41:33,774
These are my buddies from Khost.

795
00:41:34,817 --> 00:41:39,488
This picture was taken in our tent
about two weeks before.

796
00:41:41,657 --> 00:41:42,700
I spent...

797
00:41:43,951 --> 00:41:45,160
I spent 14 months

798
00:41:45,995 --> 00:41:48,122
in that tent with those guys.

799
00:41:52,376 --> 00:41:53,419
I know every inch of it.

800
00:41:54,670 --> 00:41:55,713
Good.

801
00:41:56,463 --> 00:41:58,924
Who was the first person you saw
when you woke up in the morning?

802
00:42:03,220 --> 00:42:04,263
Ford.

803
00:42:04,847 --> 00:42:06,015
Danny Ford.

804
00:42:07,433 --> 00:42:09,059
Lazy bastard's always sleeping in.

805
00:42:10,060 --> 00:42:11,645
He could sleep right through a firefight.

806
00:42:13,188 --> 00:42:14,940
Okay. Here's how it works.

807
00:42:15,816 --> 00:42:17,026
Well, let's say you need to remember

808
00:42:17,192 --> 00:42:19,403
a dentist's appointment,
Monday, 10:00 a.m.

809
00:42:20,237 --> 00:42:26,577
I want you to imagine seeing Danny
holding something ridiculous

810
00:42:26,744 --> 00:42:28,537
that makes you think of a dentist.

811
00:42:29,329 --> 00:42:31,915
- Like what, a giant tooth?
- Exactly.

812
00:42:33,167 --> 00:42:35,044
Now who was in the bunk
right next to Danny?

813
00:42:35,502 --> 00:42:37,379
Because they're gonna help you
recall the day.

814
00:42:38,464 --> 00:42:41,216
- Vasquez is.
- Okay. Can you imagine...

